// M5-A3P-1006. Ch19 I08 boss lines: Warden Hesper Oan and Ilsabet Rue (P, 9 min; ~40 words).
// act3_ch19.md §5. Two of the Abiding, held alive by bound light for four hundred years at the post the founders gave
// them: sincere, tired, certain; they believe the engine is mercy. RULE 3: fought openly as revenants for the first
// time; "revenant" may be said, never with relish. There is NO MID-BATTLE LINE HOOK yet (only lead-in barks,
// battle_transition.json): Combat plays each node at its trigger. One node per trigger.
title: ch19_bark_abiding_wardens
location: ch19/iskarra_spire
---
// The opening.
Hesper_oan as "Warden Hesper Oan" [tender]: Go home, children. We have this watch. #line:ch19_wardens_001
Ilsabet_rue as "Ilsabet Rue" [neutral]: Noted. #line:ch19_wardens_002
===
title: ch19_bark_wardens_half
---
// Hesper at 50% HP.
Hesper_oan as "Warden Hesper Oan" [sad]: Four hundred years and nobody has asked to relieve us. #line:ch19_wardens_003
===
title: ch19_bark_wardens_kerrid
---
// Once, mid-fight, if Kerrid is in the active party: the dead to the dead.
Hesper_oan as "Warden Hesper Oan" [neutral]: You kept a watch. #line:ch19_wardens_004
Kerrid [neutral]: I did. I'd have liked relieving. #line:ch19_wardens_005
===
title: ch19_bark_wardens_end
---
// Ilsabet as the last of them falls.
Ilsabet_rue as "Ilsabet Rue" [neutral]: Mark the time. #line:ch19_wardens_006
<<set $ch19_abiding_beaten = true>>
===
